 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for change delivery.** Chosen over five-second HTTPS polling (stateless and simplest to run, but leaves a few seconds of lag and repeated reads) and a hosted realtime service (least connection-ops burden, but recurring fees and provider coupling). Self-hosted WebSockets give push-speed updates without tying the board to a realtime vendor, in exchange for owning connection capacity and reconnect handling ourselves. See `docs/decisions/change-delivery-approach.md`.
